{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HSKFJcQaJ9d9XZq8nDzaRY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run for submission ===\n3\t\n4\t  - id: exp-001\n5\t    name: ner_n16_scierc\n6\t    claim: 1\n7\t    description: >\n8\t      NER N=16 on SciERC (ft_002_v2 model) to strengthen rho estimation\n9\t      and test whether increased samples push rho past 0.40.\n10\t      Also provides N-scaling data (N=8 vs N=16).\n11\t    priority: P0\n12\t    gpu_budget_hours: 6\n13\t    deps: []\n14\t    dataset: SciERC\n15\t    model: ft_002_v2\n16\t\n17\t  - id: exp-002\n18\t    name: ner_conll2003\n19\t    claim: 1\n20\t    description: >\n21\t      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on CoNLL-2003 (LoRA) + NER pilot (N=8, T=0.7)\n22\t      to validate cross-dataset generalization of Claim 1.\n23\t    priority: P0\n24\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n25\t    deps: []\n26\t    dataset: CoNLL-2003\n27\t    model: qwen3-8b (new fine-tune)\n28\t\n29\t  - id: exp-003\n30\t    name: ner_ontonotes\n31\t    claim: 1\n32\t    description: >\n33\t      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on OntoNotes 5.0 (LoRA) + NER pilot (N=8, T=0.7)\n34\t      to validate cross-dataset generalization of Claim 1.\n35\t    priority: P0\n36\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n37\t    deps: []\n38\t    dataset: OntoNotes-5.0\n39\t    model: qwen3-8b (new fine-tune)\n40\t\n41\t  - id: exp-004\n42\t    name: re_diagnostic_analysis\n43\t    claim: 2\n44\t    description: >\n45\t      Per-relation-type consistency breakdown on existing pilot_004/005 data.\n46\t      Analyze error propagation patterns: which relation types have highest/lowest\n47\t      SJ correlation, and how does this relate to type frequency and structural complexity.\n48\t    priority: P0\n49\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n50\t    deps: []\n51\t    note: CPU-only analysis on existing data\n52\t\n53\t  - id: exp-005\n54\t    name: temperature_sensitivity_analysis\n55\t    claim: 2\n56\t    description: >\n57\t      Systematic comparison of T=0.7 vs T=1.0 on both NER and RE.\n58\t      Analyze signal-noise tradeoff: T=0.7 reduces diversity (oracle headroom)\n59\t      but improves signal quality (conditional rho). Data already exists\n60\t      from pilot_004 (T=1.0) and pilot_005 (T=0.7).\n61\t    priority: P0\n62\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n63\t    deps: []\n64\t    note: CPU-only analysis on existing data\n65\t\n66\t  # === P1: Important, strongly recommended ===\n67\t\n68\t  - id: exp-006\n69\t    name: adaptive_compute_demo\n70\t    claim: 1\n71\t    description: >\n72\t      Demonstrate concrete TTS improvement on NER: compare F1 of\n73\t      SJ-based best-of-N selection vs FK-based vs random vs greedy.\n74\t      Show that SJ-guided selection outperforms alternatives.\n75\t    priority: P1\n76\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n77\t    deps: [exp-001]\n78\t    note: CPU-only, uses N=16 samples from exp-001\n79\t\n80\t  - id: exp-007\n81\t    name: ner_multi_model\n82\t    claim: 1\n83\t    description: >\n84\t      NER pilot with a different model family (LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct)\n85\t      on SciERC to show the effect is model-agnostic.\n86\t    priority: P1\n87\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n88\t    deps: []\n89\t    dataset: SciERC\n90\t    model: llama-3.1-8b (new fine-tune)\n91\t\n92\t  - id: exp-008\n93\t    name: re_n16_confirmation\n94\t    claim: 2\n95\t    description: >\n96\t      RE N=16 on SciERC to confirm negative finding with higher statistical power.\n97\t      Also tests whether N=16 changes the SJ vs FK comparison on RE.\n98\t    priority: P1\n99\t    gpu_budget_hours: 12\n100\t    deps: []\n101\t    dataset: SciERC\n102\t    model: ft_002_v2\n103\t\n104\t  - id: exp-009\n105\t    name: capability_stratification\n106\t    claim: 2\n107\t    description: >\n108\t      Stratify instances by difficulty (greedy F1 buckets) for both NER and RE.\n109\t      Analyze how rho varies across difficulty strata — does the\n110\t      capability-dependent pattern hold across subtasks?\n111\t    priority: P1\n112\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n113\t    deps: [exp-001]\n114\t    note: CPU-only analysis\n115\t\n116\t  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n117\t\n118\t  - id: exp-010\n119\t    name: selection_curves\n120\t    claim: 1\n121\t    description: >\n122\t      Best-of-N selection curves for N=1,2,4,8,16 comparing SJ vs FK vs random\n123\t      on NER. Visualize how F1 scales with compute budget under different\n124\t      confidence signals.\n125\t    priority: P2\n126\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n127\t    deps: [exp-001]\n128\t    note: CPU-only visualization\n129\t\n130\t  - id: exp-011\n131\t    name: ner_ood_robustness\n132\t    claim: 1\n133\t    description: >\n134\t      Test NER consistency signal on out-of-distribution instances\n135\t      (e.g., different domains within OntoNotes, or cross-domain transfer).\n136\t    priority: P2\n137\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n138\t    deps: [exp-003]\n139\t\n140\t# GPU Budget Summary:\n141\t# P0: 24 GPU-hours (exp-001: 6h, exp-002: 8h, exp-003: 10h, exp-004/005: 0h)\n142\t# P1: 27 GPU-hours (exp-006: 0h, exp-007: 15h, exp-008: 12h, exp-009: 0h)\n143\t# P2: 5 GPU-hours (exp-010: 0h, exp-011: 5h)\n144\t# Total P0+P1: 51 GPU-hours\n145\t# Available: 8x RTX 5090 = ~192 GPU-hours/day → P0 completable in <1 day\n146\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018vVA27REBXYzigjx1Re3NC","session_id":"f1c5840c-7d91-4900-bff4-951dfdeb834e","uuid":"a6f1d4c0-774e-4c37-9708-1270ad7a009a","timestamp":"2026-05-14T09:35:20.807Z"}
