{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MHGKYxsqYb19kEF5jsMo5A","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/docs/IDEA_BRIEF.md:**Sampling**: For each input, we sample N in {4, 8, 16, 32} schema-constrained extractions via XGrammar-backed structured generation in vLLM with temperature T=1.0 (standard for self-consistency sampling, maximizing output diversity), enforcing valid JSON output at near-zero overhead.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/docs/IDEA_BRIEF.md:10. [Temperature / 实验设计] — **增加 temperature ablation**：原始 proposal 直接采用 T=1.0 并声称 \"standard for self-consistency\"。修改为 T ∈ {0.5, 0.7, 1.0, 1.2} ablation study，分析 temperature 对 consistency-accuracy correlation、aggregation quality、gating accuracy 的影响，承认 T=1.0 是 reasoning task 标准但可能不适用于 fine-tuned IE 模型。 — 命中 Technical Soundness\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/registry.yaml:        --data_dir data/scierc --dataset scierc --subtask joint --n_samples 8 --temperature\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/registry.yaml:        --dataset scierc --subtask joint --n_samples 8 --temperature 1.0 --max_tokens\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/registry.yaml:        8 --temperature 1.0 --max_tokens 1024 --output_dir output/mvp_pilot_004 --num_test\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/registry.yaml:        8 --temperature 0.7 --max_tokens 1024 --output_dir output/mvp_pilot_005 --num_test\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/experiment_plan.yaml:    name: temperature_sensitivity_analysis\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/paper_framing.md:- **Mitigation**: Frame Claim 2 as diagnostic contribution — identifying WHY and WHEN consistency fails is as valuable as showing it works. Component decomposition + temperature sensitivity provide mechanistic explanation.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018vVA27REBXYzigjx1Re3NC","session_id":"f1c5840c-7d91-4900-bff4-951dfdeb834e","uuid":"2d52caff-168b-4f22-9e09-c0544d17e387","timestamp":"2026-05-14T09:35:39.041Z"}
